/**
\page editM Edit Menu

\anchor idx_Edit_Menu_145

![](medit.png)

The <b>Edit Menu</b> shows commands affecting the <b>Main Canvas</b> (\ref mainW).

- <i>Undo</i> \anchor idx_Undo_146  - Reverses the last command.  Up to the last ten commands can be undone.  If there are no commands that can be undone the <b>Undo</b> item is disabled.  The <b>Undo</b> command can also be invoked by the <b>Undo</b> button (\ref cmdUndo).

- <i>Redo</i> \anchor idx_Redo_147  - Undoes the last Undo command.  The <b>Redo</b> command can also be invoked by the <b>Redo</b> button (\ref cmdUndo).

- <i>Cut</i> \anchor idx_Cut_148  - Moves the selected objects to the clipboard.

- <i>Copy</i> \anchor idx_Copy_149  - Copies the selected objects to the clipboard.

- <i>Paste</i> \anchor idx_Paste_150  - Copies the contents of the clipboard to the layout. Using the paste Menu command it will be placed at the center of the screen.
If the context menu paste is used or the short-cuts <i>Ctrl+v</i> or <i>Shift+Insert</i>, the parts will be placed at the cursor position.
Repeated Pastes without moving the cursor result in overlaid copies.
The newly pasted parts are in <b>Selected</b> state and can easily be moved into place. Any previously selected objects are unselected.

- <i>Delete</i> \anchor idx_Delete_151  - Deletes the selected objects.

- <i>Move To Current Layer</i> \anchor idx_Move_To_Current_Layer_152  - move all selected objects to the current Layer (\ref cmdLayer).

- <i>Select All</i> \anchor idx_Select_All_153  - Selects all objects on the layout.

- <i>Select Current Layer</i> \anchor idx_Select_Current_Layer_154  - selects all objects in the current Layer (\ref cmdLayer).

- <i>Select By Index</i> \anchor idx_Select_By_Index_155  - selects object by index number (\ref cmdSelectIndex).

- <i>Deselect All</i> \anchor idx_Deselect_All_156  - unselects all objects on the layout. The same action can be achieved by pressing the ESC key.

- <i>Invert Selection</i> \anchor idx_Invert_Selection_157  - selects all unselected objects and unselects all previously selected objects.

- <i>Select Stranded Track</i> \anchor idx_Select_Stranded_Track_158  - selects all track pieces that are not connected to any other objects. This helps cleaning up a drawing after many changes have been made.

- <i>Tunnel</i> \anchor idx_Tunnel_159 \anchor idx_Track_Tunnel_160  - Hides or reveals selected tracks and adds a tunnel portal symbol where the track passes from one to the other.

- <i>Bridge</i> \anchor idx_Bridge_161 \anchor idx_Track_Bridge_162  - Adds or removes parapet symbols and a solid base to the track. The color is selectable (\ref cmdRgbcolor).

- <i>Roadbed</i> \anchor idx_Roadbed_163 \anchor idx_Track_Roadbed_164  - Adds or removes solid roadbed under the track. The color is selectable (\ref cmdRgbcolor).

- <i>Ties/No Ties</i> \anchor idx_Ties_No_Ties_165 \anchor idx_Track_Ties_166 \anchor idx_Track_No_Ties_167  - Hides or reveals the ties on selected tracks.

- <i>Move To Front</i> \anchor idx_Move_To_Front_168  - Moves selected object to foreground.

- <i>Move To Back</i> \anchor idx_Move_To_Back_169  - Moves selected object to background.

- <i>Thin, Medium and Thick Tracks</i> \anchor idx_Thin_Medium_and_Thick_Tracks_170  \anchor idx_Thin_Tracks_171 \anchor idx_Medium_Tracks_172 
	\anchor idx_Thick_Tracks_173 \anchor idx_Tracks_Thin_174 \anchor idx_Tracks_Medium_175 \anchor idx_Tracks_Thick_176 
	\anchor idx_Track_Width_177 
	- set displayed rail width of selected tracks.

For more information on working with selected objects, see the Select (\ref cmdSelect) command.

- \subpage cmdSelectIndex
- \subpage cmdAboveBelow
- \subpage addshortcutkeys
- \subpage cmdDelete
- \subpage cmdTunnel
- \subpage cmdTies
- \subpage cmdBridge
- \subpage cmdRoadbed
- \subpage cmdUndo

*/

/**
\page cmdSelectIndex Select By Index

\anchor idx_Select_By_Index_178

An input window allows one or more index numbers to be entered. Multiple indexes are seperated by commas.

The object can not be selected if its Layer is frozen.

If the object is part of a module layer, all objects in the layer will be selected.

If the object is a tunnel object, and the Display Tunnel option is None, it will be set to Dashed. See Display options (\ref cmdDisplay).

When an individual object is selected, its index number is displayed in the Info Message area, another source is the List Parts (\ref cmdEnum) command with the <b>List Indexes</b> option.

*/

/**
\page cmdAboveBelow "Move To Front" and "Move to Back"  

\anchor idx_Move_To_Front_179
\anchor idx_Move_To_Back_180

![](btop_bottom.png)

The Move to Front and Move To Back commands move the selected objects (\ref cmdSelect) to the top of the drawing list - the <b>Foreground</b> or to the bottom of the list - the <b>Background</b> making them more or less visible or prominent.

The effect is to make the objects move to be in front of all or behind all other objects.  This command is useful when dealing with filled shapes (\ref cmdDraw).

Selected objects moved to the <b>Background</b> become unselected.

*/

/**
\page addshortcutkeys Additional Shortcut Keys

\anchor idx_Additional_Shortcut_Keys_181

Additional Shortcut keys perform the following:

- `Ctrl+Z` - Undo

- `Ctrl+R` - Redo

- `Ctrl+C` - Copy

- `Ctrl+V` - Paste

- `Ctrl+X` - Cut

- `Esc` - Deselect All

*/

/**
\page cmdDelete Delete

\anchor idx_Delete_182

![](bdelete.png)

The <b>Delete</b> button is used to delete selected objects.  Remember, the <b>Undo</b> (\ref editM or \ref cmdUndo) command can be used to restore a delete object.

Deleting a track that is connected to an easement (\ref cmdEasement) causes the easement to be deleted as well.

The <i>Delete</i> key invokes the Delete command.

*/

/**
\page cmdTunnel Tunnel (Hide Tracks)

\anchor idx_Tunnel_Hide_Tracks_183

![](btunnel.png)

The <b>Tunnel</b> command is used to hide selected (\ref cmdSelect) tracks (as in a tunnel).

Select the tracks you want to hide in a tunnel.  Selecting a hidden track 'reveals' it.

A tunnel portal is drawn where a hidden track connects with an 'unhidden' track.  You can split (\ref cmdSplitTrack) a track to place a tunnel portal at a particular spot.

The <b>Draw Tunnels</b> Radio button group on the <b>Options&gt;Display</b> dialog (\ref cmdDisplay) controls whether hidden tracks are not drawn, drawn as dashed lines or drawn as normal lines.

*/

/**
\page cmdTies Ties (Draw or Hide Ties)

\anchor idx_Ties_Draw_or_Hide_Ties_184

![](bties.png)

The <b>Ties</b> command is used to hide Ties (or reshow them).  This may be useful for overlapping track, like dual gauge, or in areas like docks or yards where the track is covered.

Select the tracks you want to hide or show ties for.

*/

/**
\page cmdBridge Bridge (Draw or Hide Abutments)

\anchor idx_Bridge_Draw_or_Hide_Abutments_185

![](bbridge.png)

The <b>Bridge</b> command is used to add abutments to a track (as on an underbridge).

Select the tracks you want to be a bridge. Bridge abutments are drawn alongside the track and a solid layer is added under the ties. You can split (\ref cmdSplitTrack) a track to shorten the length of the bridge, or to add an extra pier to the drawing.

If you perform this action on an existing bridge (or use Tunnel) the bridge is removed.

*/

/**
\page cmdRoadbed Roadbed (Draw or Hide Base)

\anchor idx_Roadbed_Draw_or_Hide_Base_186

![](broadbed.png)

The <b>Roadbed</b> command is used to add a solid color under a track (as roadbed).

Select the tracks you want to have roadbed. A solid roadbed layer is drawn under the track.

If you perform this action on existing roadbed (or use Tunnel) the roadbed is removed. The bridge option takes precedence over roadbed.

*/

/**
\page cmdUndo Undo and Redo  

\anchor idx_Undo_187
\anchor idx_Redo_188

![](bgundo.png)

The <b>Undo</b> and <b>Redo</b> buttons invoke the same actions as the <b>Edit</b> menu items.  The name of last command will be displayed as the Balloon Help (\ref windowTerms) for the <i>Undo</i> button.  The name of last undone command will be displayed as the Balloon Help for the <i>Redo</i> button.

*/

